mission "Black Sails at Dawn"
    name "Black Sails at Dawn"
    description "Carry Tortuga's warning to Havana before a pirate squadron reaches the harbour."
    source "Tortuga"
    destination "Havana"
    reward 350
    speaker offer "Marta, the Tavern Keeper"
    speaker visit "Havana Harbour Commander"
    speaker complete "Havana Harbour Commander"
    to offer
        has "A Map in the Bottle: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Marta bars the tavern door behind you. The room smells of rum, wet rope, and woodsmoke. She unrolls a scrap of sailcloth marked with three black crosses.`
            `"Those are the colours of Captain Vane. His ships have been gathering in the cays, and a lookout saw them steering for Havana. The governor there thinks the old walls will keep him safe. They won't, not without warning."`
            choice
                `"I'll take the warning to Havana."`
                    goto accept_job
                `"How many ships has Vane gathered?"`
                    goto details
                `"I'm no messenger. Count me out."`
                    goto decline_job
            label details
                `"Three that we know of," Marta says. "A brig, a sloop, and a little gunboat that bites like a shark. Vane wants the harbour's silver fleet. Reach Havana before dawn and they'll have time to close the chain across the channel."`
                choice
                    `"Then I'll make all sail for Havana."`
                        goto accept_job
                    `"I won't risk my ship for the governor."`
                        goto decline_job
            label accept_job
                `Marta presses a wax-sealed letter into your hand. "Give this to the harbour commander. Don't stop for cards, drink, or trouble. Especially trouble."`
                accept
            label decline_job
                `Marta folds the marked sailcloth and slips it beneath the counter. "Then may the wind be kinder to Havana than Vane will be."`
                close
    on accept
        log "Accepted Marta's warning run. Deliver her sealed letter to Havana."
    on visit
        conversation
            `The harbour commander breaks Marta's seal. His expression hardens. "All hands to the guns! Raise the harbour chain and clear the channel!"`
            `Bells begin clanging along the seawall. Far beyond the reefs, black sails appear against the red morning sky, but the harbour is ready. Vane's squadron veers away under a hail of warning shot.`
    on complete
        conversation
            `The commander clasps your forearm. "You got here in time. Havana owes you more than a purse of gold." He glances toward the eastern sea. "Vane's scouts are still out there. We need a captain willing to hunt them down before they return."`
        log "Havana was warned before Vane's squadron arrived. The harbour is safe for now."
